   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "id": "",
    "nodes": [],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "id": "",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "id": "",
      "nodes": [],
      "textData": {
       "text": "The answer was ",
       "decorations": []
      }
     },
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "id": "",
      "nodes": [],
      "textData": {
       "text": "Grid-Break",
       "decorations": [
        {
         "type": "BOLD",
         "fontWeightValue": 700
        }
       ]
      }
     },
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "id": "",
      "nodes": [],
      "textData": {
       "text": ", which is likely to become the game's signature. When the Grid-Break gauge fills in the middle of a battle, the grid and the turns vanish and the team fights in real time for a short while, empowered. It's touch-only, and it rewards skill, not speed: perfect chains, dodges and guard breaks, while mashing makes the crew fumble.",
       "decorations": []
      }
     }
    ],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "id": "",
    "nodes": [],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
    "type": "PARAGRAPH",
    "id": "",
    "nodes": [
     {
      "type": "TEXT",
      "id": "",
      "nodes": [],
      "textData": {
       "text": "That gave one fight three modes. The grid is the hub, for tactics against many foes. A swarm plus a full gauge means Grid-Break. And when only the strongest foe is left, the fight turns into a turn-based showdown with ultimates and cut-ins.",
       "decorations": []
      }
     }
    ],
    "paragraphData": {}
   },
   {
